WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.800
Technicians should not have to stop
working just to search
across business systems.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.900
Flo turns Alexa+ into a hands-free
operating layer, grounded in real tools.

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:17.500
This custom Alexa+ simulation exposes
Flo's live MCP connection,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.850
persistent job context, transaction guard,
and optional tool trace.

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:25.700
Open work order 1842.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.700
Flo retrieves the assigned Ford F-150

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.300
and its complaint through structured
MCP tools.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.000
The alternator failed.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.900
Flo records the diagnosis,
checks deterministic fitment,

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.600
searches three simulated suppliers,
and displays compatible offers.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.100
The trace also shows
a live Amazon Bedrock narration call.

00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:55.900
Bedrock contributes only
a concise qualitative lead.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.300
Deterministic code still ranks
every option and calculates
the exact shop cost,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.300
customer price, warranty, delivery,
and margin.

00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:09.300
Add the recommended part to the estimate
and request approval.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:16.300
Flo calculates $459.03, then stores
the customer request as pending.

00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:20.200
A demo control simulates
the customer response.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:26.800
Approval is now stored,
but no supplier order or schedule change
has been executed.

00:01:27.335 --> 00:01:31.400
In a fresh conversation,
ask what happened with the Ford.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:38.250
Flo resolves the recent job
and reports the approval,
without inventing new transaction state.

00:01:38.809 --> 00:01:42.000
Now order the alternator
and schedule Bay 2 tomorrow morning.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.200
Flo rechecks approval,
supplier availability, and the bay,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.300
then presents the exact action.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.600
Nothing happens yet.

00:01:53.142 --> 00:01:57.100
Only after a separate Confirm
does the server place the order,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.500
reserve Bay 2, update the work order,
and write audit records.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:06.900
Single-use tokens and idempotency
prevent accidental repeats.

00:02:07.424 --> 00:02:11.900
Flo uses MCP 2025-11-25
over Streamable HTTP,

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.700
with thin handlers, an orchestrator,
deterministic engines,
and replaceable adapters.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.500
The verified Lambda-to-Bedrock
path is live;

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.600
AgentCore and DynamoDB remain
clearly labeled roadmap items.

00:02:28.124 --> 00:02:33.100
Flo is MIT licensed,
publicly available, and built to extend
beyond automotive repair.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:40.750
Hands-free service operations,
with every important action
inspectable and safe.
